From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Altera BMC <openbmc@altera.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon-temp: add P3T1755 to sensorTypes

The NXP P3T1755 is the temperature sensor on the MikroE Thermo 10 Click
(MIKROE-6771) used in the Step 1 demo. The Linux lm75 driver supports it
natively (i2c device id "p3t1755", compatible "nxp,p3t1755", and native
I3C via module_i3c_i2c_driver), but hwmontempsensor's sensorTypes map did
not list it, so an entity-manager "P3T1755" Exposes entry was ignored.

Add the type so dbus-sensors instantiates the device with driver name
"p3t1755" (createsHWMon = true) and publishes its temperature on D-Bus.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Altera BMC <openbmc@altera.com>
---
 src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp b/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
index d43a6d0..8fa9c9f 100644
--- a/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
+++ b/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ static const I2CDeviceTypeMap sensorTypes{
     {"MCP9600", I2CDeviceType{"mcp9600", false}},
     {"NCT6779", I2CDeviceType{"nct6779", true}},
     {"NCT7802", I2CDeviceType{"nct7802", true}},
+    {"P3T1755", I2CDeviceType{"p3t1755", true}},
     {"PT5161L", I2CDeviceType{"pt5161l", true}},
     {"SBTSI", I2CDeviceType{"sbtsi", true}},
     {"SBRMI", I2CDeviceType{"sbrmi", true}},
